{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"Release-note text for this story (moved out of the description to keep it under the 8,000-char admission cap; docs/release-notes.md carries it verbatim):\n\nRelease note (BREAKING, pre-1.0): the legacy HMAC-SHA256 signing scheme is retired. `REBAR_SIGNING_KEY` and `<tracker>/.signing-key` are no longer read (`rebar init` stops creating the file; delete yours); every SIGNATURE record without a DSSE `envelope` (all attestations minted before 2026-07-15) now verifies `unsigned` with reason `legacy HMAC scheme retired (2026-09); re-run the gate to mint an op-cert`, no longer `unknown_scheme` or `foreign_key`; closed tickets are unaffected; an open ticket holding one needs one `rebar review-plan`; `rebar.signing.{signing_key, key_fingerprint, compute_signature, verify_record, ALGORITHM, PAYLOAD_VERSION}` are removed from the library surface and `verify_attestation_record` loses its `key` parameter."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1792360556085788001,"uuid":"231a625b-3adb-4626-b6ed-6b4d8e9a6ba3"}